ROM images (machines/rk86/roms/monitor.bin, font.bin), not the owner's work and not relicensed:
- monitor.bin: the monitor of the Radio-86RK, published in Radio magazine (Moscow), 1986, by the
  authors of the Radio-86RK design, D. Gorshkov, G. Zelenko, Yu. Ozerov and S. Popov. Not yet
  checked against the published listing or a dump of an original ROM.
- font.bin: the character generator of the Radio-86RK; its authorship and publication are not
  established (open).
Where the stored copies come from and their licence status: machines/rk86/roms/PROVENANCE.md
(the only licence statement found for them names LICENSES/LicenseRef-Tselikov-BSD.txt; the status
of the original publication is open).

The IC models that the machines instantiate are in retroICs (the submodule lib/retroICs); their
authors, origins and licences are in the NOTICE of retroICs.

Builds: a bitstream or netlist built from a machine of this repo carries the owner's copyright line
and the licence (LICENSE) and the attribution line above. It also includes the IC models of
retroICs, so it carries the NOTICE of retroICs as well. ROM images loaded with it keep their own
status and the credit above.
